Carafe bench: a texture buffer GL can't view directly is read from a copy. glTextureBufferRange needs an offset
that is a multiple of GL_TEXTURE_BUFFER_OFFSET_ALIGNMENT (256 on Mesa d3d12, 16 on the guest's GPU); otherwise
it fails with GL_INVALID_VALUE, the view keeps no buffer and reads zeros, and Mesa's pixel-buffer uploads in the
guest (OpenTTD's OpenGL video and animation buffers) came out black. Buffer textures also have no swizzle, so a
B8G8R8A8 view (patch 0014) read as RGBA8 had red and blue swapped. The range is copied to the start of a scratch
buffer, and B8G8R8A8 texels get red and blue swapped there by a compute shader.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

